;; Copy for context. Text and inline HSX-compatible markup.
(:title
 ("Read beyond " (:em nil "one context window."))
 :prose
 ("You can ask Autolith to process data that is too large to fit in the conversation. Autolith uses " (:a (:href "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.24601" :class "ulink") "recursive language models") " to partition and recombine large contexts.")
 :prose-2
 ("The agent gets a structured inspectable trace it can use to produce an answer." (:br nil) (:br nil) "The number of model requests, the number of tokens and the depth of recursion can by limited by you (if you invoke RLM manually), or the agent. If a run reaches a limit, it can be resumed with an additional budget, so that we do not waste any tokens."))
